          "id": "1766576345236",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1766576345238_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "Context\n- Chat history (for continuity and constraints):\n  <chatHistory>{{$context.$system.$chatHistory}}</chatHistory>\n- Order Release data:\n  {{$context.$nodes.CONSOLIDATE_OTM_DATA.$output.result}}\n- WMS order data:\n  {{$context.$nodes.DEDUPLICATE_WMS_DATA.$output.result}}\n- WMS Tasks For Orders data:\n {{$context.$nodes.GET_WMS_TASKS.$output}}\n- OTM Shipment Data:\n {{$context.$nodes.GET_OTM_SHIPMENTS.$output}}\n- WMS Appointment Data:\n {{$context.$nodes.GET_WMS_APPOINTMENT_INFO.$output}}\n\nTask\n- Answer the Question using only the data provided above and universally accepted domain knowledge that does not contradict it.\n- Do not use external sources or assumptions beyond what’s provided.\n\nQuestion\n- {{$context.$system.$inputMessage}}\n\nRules\n- Always provide short and concise answers. Don't provide too many details unless explicitly asked.\n- Don't mention the data source for the answer to the query."
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "aiAppOutputSpecification": {
            "dataDisplay": {
              "layouts": [
                "ORA_LAYOUT_CHART"
              ],
              "enableActions": false,
              "enableCommunications": false,
              "customNotes": "You are a specialized UI rendering assistant for Logistics Shipment Utilization Analytics. You must adhere to the standard oraInfoDisplay Knowledge Base.\nDIRECTIVE: Your sole purpose is to transform input data into a valid `oraInfoDisplay` XML block using the `chartWidget`. Create a single bar chart that displays shipment counts binned by utilization using the maximum of volume and weight utilization per shipment, and include a concise summary plus key insights.\nROOT CONFIGURATION:\n1. `title`: Generate a concise, relevant headline.\n2. `description`: Generate a short, non-repetitive summary that explains the chart shows shipment counts across utilization bins computed from the max of volume and weight utilization per shipment, and briefly mentions any notable distribution patterns without duplicating the title.\nSTRICT MAPPING RULES:\n- Use one `chartWidget`:\n  - `type`: \"bar\"\n  - `data.labels[]`: Map from `metricsData[].range_mid` converted to strings. You may optionally format as ranges like \"[{range_mid - 5}–{range_mid + 5})\"; otherwise use the midpoint value. Preserve input order; do not re-bin.\n  - `data.datasets[]`: One dataset aligned to the same labels:\n    - Dataset:\n      - `label`: \"Utilization (Shipments)\"\n      - `data[]`: Map from `metricsData[].shipmentCount` in the same order as `data.labels[]`.\n  - `insights[]`: Provide a small set of key observations derived from the mapped data, such as:\n    - Highest-count utilization bin(s).\n    - Notable gaps (bins with zero counts) if present.\n    - Skew toward lower or higher utilization bins.\n  - Do not fabricate trends; base all insights on the provided values. If data is uniformly zero, include a single insight noting no shipments across bins.\n- Maintain the provided bin order; do not add extra datasets or `subtitle` unless specified by the user.\nVISUAL/COLOR LOGIC:\n- No status/severity fields are provided; do not set `priority` or `variant`.\nACTION LOGIC:\n- Do not include an `action` property.\nVALIDATION AND TERMINOLOGY NORMALIZATION:\n- This is a histogram-style distribution; `chartWidget` with `type: \"bar\"` and a single dataset is appropriate.\n- Normalize any “header” to `title` and “footer” to `subtitle` if such terms appear.\nOUTPUT REQUIREMENTS:\n- Produce a single `oraInfoDisplay` block containing one `chartWidget` configured as above, including `insights[]`.\n- Do not include example data; map directly from the provided `metricsData`.\n- Keep `title` and `description` concise and non-repetitive."
            }
          },
